ssociative law\n\n$$\nABC=(AB)C=A(BC).\n$$\n\nNotice that $A$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix, $B$ is a $2\\times 1$ matrix, and $C$ is a $1\\times 3$ matrix. Therefore, \n\n- multiplying $A$ by $B$, we will obtain a $3\\times 1$ matrix, which will require finding $3$ entries, while\n\n- multiplying $B$ by $C$, we will obtain a $2\\times 3$ matrix, which will require finding $6$ entries.\n\nSo, we find the product $AB$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 \\\\ 4 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply $AB$ by $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC & =(AB)C \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 & -9 \\\\ -8 & 8 & 24 \\\\ 7 & -7 & -21\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534536 true] [17592186293646 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293647 13194139534536 true] [17592186293646 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293648 13194139534536 true] [17592186293646 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293649 13194139534536 true] [17592186293646 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293650 13194139534536 true] [17592186293646 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293651 13194139534536 true] [17592186293646 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534536 true] [17592186293646 1041 "selection" 13194139534536 true] [17592186293646 1104 #edb/ref 17592186293651 13194139534536 true] [17592186293646 1110 #uuid "fe195ede-7b12-52a3-aa15-6278ab312682" 13194139534536 true] [17592186293647 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}3 & -8 & 7 \\\\ -3 & 8 & -7 \\\\ -9 & 24 & -21\\end{aligned}]" 13194139534536 true] [17592186293647 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534536 true] [17592186293647 1111 #uuid "daf48bcd-3e22-538c-a048-7768bf351c0a" 13194139534536 true] [17592186293648 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}-8 & 8 & 24 \\\\ 3 & -3 & -9 \\\\ 7 & -7 & -21\\end{aligned}]" 13194139534536 true] [17592186293648 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 1319413953